// Test: bugfixes/list_namespace_functions_check_element_type
// Grammar: namespace_call
// Semantic: SEM001 — `list.f(items, ...)` is the namespace form of
//   `items.f(...)`; its values must have the list's element type
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.183
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:20
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:21
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:22
//   list_namespace_functions_check_element_type.cln:19
//   A value of type string cannot be used as integer
//
// Regression: `list.add(numbers, "zz")` stored a string pointer in a list of
// integers (`l[2]` printed an address).

start:
	list<integer> l = [1, 2]
	list.add(l, "zz")
	list.set(l, 0, "zz")
	list.insert(l, 0, "zz")
	boolean b = list.contains(l, "zz")
	print(b.toString())
